.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_character_tables \- set character tables
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_set_character_tables(\fBpcre2_compile_context\fP *\fIccontext\fP,
                               \fBconst\fP \fBuint8_t\fP *\fItables\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function sets a pointer to custom character tables within a compile
context. The second argument must point to a set of PCRE2 character tables or
be \f(CRNULL\fP to request the default tables. The result is always zero. Character
tables can be created by calling pcre2_maketables() or by running the
\f(CRpcre2_dftables\fP maintenance command in binary mode (see the
\f(CRpcre2build\fP
documentation).
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.